            "review_text": "b.s.y.c\nJakarta, Indonesia275 contributions\n0\nA very nice chicken curry in town!\nDec 2017 • Solo\nFound this restaurant when I explored the Backpacker street and saw a group of young students having dinner there.\nThere are variety of local Vietnamese, Asian, Western menu. I finally chose \"chicken soup\", \"Chicken curry served with a bowl of steamed rice\" and one can of Sprite. They served both chicken curry and chicken soup at the same time, even I expected the chicken soup to be served as appetizer. It tasted very nice with chicken meats, creamy soup and mushrooms, served with three pieces of toasted bread. As main course, the chicken curry tasted very delicious, perfect combination with potatoes, onions and vegetables. The curry itself is not thick or creamy, perfect balance for me. I even told te waitress that the chicken curry is the queen of the night. The price overall is considered as quite expensive, however, I think it's worthy and recommended restaurant to try at least once.\nRead more\nWritten December 13, 2017",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-13",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
